From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenBook <noreply@anybook.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: TerminalApp: the agent bridge starts the Linux
 environment

AgentBridgeProvider gets call("start"): when the Linux environment is
stopped (after every reboot) or failed, it starts the VM; when it isn't
installed, it installs it (from the image a debuggable build finds in
/sdcard/linux, else the download) and starts the VM once installed.
status() reports "installing" while the installer runs.

So Quire core can start its agents' environment when the person calls
it, and the person never has to open the Terminal app for that. Both
paths start VmService, a foreground service: the caller exempts this
app from the background start limit first; a start that fails anyway is
reported as an error, not a crash.

OpenBook ANAL-225 (Quire on the G14).

Change-Id: Ic9ea0c53eb6bff036ac8ab85346aaccbef92e5af
